{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793599905,"nonce":"sfcx0f3t1byo9XqS4pBL7GIL5ss=","message":"Scope and exit criterion changed after the 2026-11-01 roadmap review (design §11 and §12 updated to match).\n\nScope additions:\n\n- Moved from M4: well-founded recursion with `Spec.Decreases` (omega discharges the decrease obligations), quantified theorems, and the `Prove` syntax. Differential tests of WF-recursive units need an evaluation strategy other than kernel whnf (for example unfolding equation lemmas).\n- A development-time export of the simp lemma set, instances and reducibility attributes for the pinned Init/Std/semantics bundle, as a versioned sidecar next to the NDJSON bundle. lean4export carries none of this, and the ported `simp`, instance synthesis and M8's `grind` need it. It is untrusted tactic input, hashed into the store manifest and the cache key.\n\nExit criterion gains: the certificate of a verified C# theorem exports and passes `scripts/cross-check.sh` (D6 has not been tested on translated code before).\n\nOpen questions retimed: decide Q8's fuel and time budgets and Q9 (CI trust policy) when M5 starts, because the server enforces the budgets and the MSBuild task is authoritative for CI.\n\nStill open: whether to split M5 or strengthen its exit criterion. Being decided separately.","files":null}]}